From: Long Way Home <noreply@long-way-home.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] the dead are not reloaded

One attach point and its no-op. In the ship programme death is attrition, not a reload:
docs/path-to-playtest.md Stage B asks that the player's death be reachable and *not* a reload.
Retail's respawn (press attack while dead) sends `load *respawn`, which under ironman resumes the
one forward save -- a reset all the same. This hook lets the player-in-the-world logic refuse it:
when the extension is on and the player's record is closed, respawn does nothing, and the ship
carries on with command passed to the senior surviving officer.

The logic is not in this tree: `LWH_BlockRespawn` is compiled in from LWH_MODULE_DIR (which defines
LWH_CREW). Without it the hook is an empty inline returning false, so the module builds and behaves
exactly as upstream does.
---
diff --git a/efgame/src/game/g_client.cpp b/efgame/src/game/g_client.cpp
--- a/efgame/src/game/g_client.cpp
+++ b/efgame/src/game/g_client.cpp
@@ -3,6 +3,8 @@
 #include "anims.h"
 #include "boltons.h"
 
+#include "lwh_hooks.h"
+
 extern void Q3_DebugPrint( int level, const char *format, ... );
 // g_client.c -- client functions that don't happen every frame
 
@@ -303,6 +305,11 @@
 */
 void respawn( gentity_t *ent ) {
 
+	if ( LWH_BlockRespawn( ent ) ) {
+		// the record is closed and the extension is on: the dead are not reloaded (Stage B)
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if (Q_stricmpn(level.mapname,"_holo",5)) {
 		gi.SendConsoleCommand("load *respawn\n");	// special case
 	}
diff --git a/efgame/src/game/lwh_hooks.h b/efgame/src/game/lwh_hooks.h
--- a/efgame/src/game/lwh_hooks.h
+++ b/efgame/src/game/lwh_hooks.h
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
 inline const char *LWH_ScopedName( const char *name ) { return name; }
 inline void LWH_SP_target_shaderremap( struct gentity_s * ) {}
 inline void LWH_target_shaderremap_use( struct gentity_s *, struct gentity_s *, struct gentity_s * ) {}
+inline bool LWH_BlockRespawn( struct gentity_s * ) { return false; }
 #endif
 
 #endif
